<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
   GROMACS code registration.

   STATUS: PRESENT BUT NOT REGISTERED. Neither ResourceDescriptor.xml nor
   ResourceDescriptorRxn.xml references this code, so no "New GROMACS
   Calculation..." menu entry exists and no calculation of this type can
   be created. That is deliberate: registering it forces the scope
   decision in issue #106, which is the maintainer's to make. See
   docs/GROMACS_ROADMAP.md.

   CodeFactory::getCodes() scans this directory, so the file being here
   does make GROMACS appear in code lists that are built by directory
   scan (notably CalcEd's code-switch buttons, via
   getFullySupportedCodes(), since both InputGenerator and Template are
   present). That is the intended state for groundwork: reachable to
   inspect, not reachable to create.

   SCOPE: IMPORT-ONLY. GROMACS takes three inputs - .mdp (run control),
   .top (topology and force field) and .gro (coordinates) - and grompp
   combines them into a binary .tpr that mdrun executes. Only the .mdp is
   generated here. The topology is the user's, brought in from pdb2gmx or
   elsewhere and attached with File > Upload File.

   ECCE has no concept of a force field, and inventing one is a much
   larger piece of work than this: see section 3.1 of the roadmap.

   THE .tpr IS A BUILD ARTEFACT, not the input file. <DataFiles> declares
   the .mdp as the primary input because that is what ECCE generates and
   the user edits. gromacs.launchpp runs grompp at launch time to produce
   the .tpr, and surfaces grompp's diagnostics rather than discarding
   them - a mismatched topology is the first thing a new user hits, and
   grompp says exactly what is wrong.

   NO <Importer>: a GROMACS.expt for externally-run jobs is not written,
   so GROMACS correctly does not appear in CodeFactory::getImportCodes().

   NOTE ON ".top": NWChem already claims that extension as
   chemical/x-nwchem-topology in packaging/dataserver/httpd.conf.ecce,
   and GROMACS uses it for its own topology. Whoever registers this code
   has to decide how to disambiguate; a second AddType would silently
   change what NWChem MD topologies resolve to.

   Verified end to end against real GROMACS 2025.2: ai.gromacs generated
   the .mdp, grompp built the .tpr, mdrun ran, and gromacs.desc parsed
   the resulting log back into TE/TEVEC.
-->
<appdescriptor>

<!-- GROMACS constrains bonds and angles through the .mdp "constraints"
     setting, which the Runtype Details dialog exposes for dynamics.
     That is not the same thing as ECCE's geometry-constraint editor,
     which is about freezing internal coordinates during an optimisation
     and which ai.gromacs does not write. Declared false rather than
     advertising a capability the generator drops. -->
<SupportsConstraints>false</SupportsConstraints>

<!-- No basis sets: GROMACS is a classical molecular dynamics code and
     has none. needsBasis="false" is the pre-existing mechanism for this
     (NWChem's NWPW theories and MOPAC's semiempirical ones both use
     it): CalcEd greys out the Basis Set Tool, and ESInputController
     skips the .basis file and the BasisSet.Coordinates key entirely.
     CodeFactory::getBasisCodes() also filters GROMACS out because
     <GaussianBasisSetRules> is absent. No C++ change was needed. -->
<Editor theorydialog="gromacstheory.py" runtypedialog="gromacsruntype.py">
  <Theory category="MD" name="MD" needsBasis="false">
    <runtype>Energy</runtype>
    <runtype>Geometry</runtype>
    <runtype>Dynamics</runtype>
  </Theory>

  <TheorySummary topLabel="Molecular Dynamics-">
    <item key="ES.Theory.MD.Coulombtype" label="Electrostatics"></item>
  </TheorySummary>
  <TheorySummary>
    <item key="ES.Theory.MD.CoulombCutoff" label="Coulomb Cutoff (nm)"></item>
  </TheorySummary>
</Editor>

<!-- The .mdp extension is distinctive and has an AddType in
     packaging/dataserver/httpd.conf.ecce. That matters at UPLOAD time
     rather than registration time: a file with no MIME mapping becomes
     "DefaultType text/plain", and ECCE's mimetype-filtered lookup for a
     calculation's primary input then cannot match it even though the
     file is on disk - which looks exactly like a save failure. -->
<DataFiles>
  <Input  type="primary" mimetype="chemical/x-gromacs-mdp" comment="true" commentstring=";">gromacs.mdp</Input>
  <Output type="primary" mimetype="chemical/x-gromacs-log">gromacs.log</Output>
  <Output type="parse" verifypattern="GROMACS:" mimetype="chemical/x-gromacs-log">gromacs.log</Output>
</DataFiles>

<!-- <LaunchPreprocessor> is required unconditionally:
     Launch::postProcessInput() shells out to JCode::launchPPScript()
     with no empty-string check, so a code without one fails launch with
     a bare "-p postParams" command-not-found. Here it has real work to
     do - running grompp. -->
<IntegrationFiles>
  <Template>gromacs.tpl</Template>
  <InputGenerator>ai.gromacs</InputGenerator>
  <ParseSpecification>gromacs.desc</ParseSpecification>
  <LaunchPreprocessor>gromacs.launchpp</LaunchPreprocessor>
</IntegrationFiles>

</appdescriptor>
